$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^2-16}{x^2+4x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{(x+4)(x-4)}{x(x+4)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{{}\cancel{(x+4)}(x-4)}{{x}\cancel{(x+4)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x-4}{x}, \text{ for }x\neq -4 
\end{align}$
